{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_exuabrj4g5gyferefyfn6qsfazhez3qzkewlvk363pyofsi25ceq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_019NqurGU2t9YtfLAgzRqkQ3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-6AvRo1/translation/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — Configuration surface (valid inputs)\n\n## Axes the C code actually branches on\n\nDerived from `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`, `c_src/src/mdmacros.h` and the `#ifdef` /\n`switch` / token-paste sites in `c_src/src/mdcore.c`:\n\n### Build-time axes (the *only* \"options\" this API has — there is no runtime setter)\n\n| axis | source | domain | what it toggles |\n|------|--------|--------|-----------------|\n| `OP` | `CMakeLists.txt:26` `set(OP \"add\" …)`; `mdmacros.h:27` fallback `add` | `add`, `sub`, `mul` | `OP_FN(OP)` → which `op_*` is called; `STEP_<OP>` (`+=i` / `-=i` / `*=(i+1)`); `INIT_<OP>` (`0`/`0`/`1`); `STR(OP)` → `G_OP_NAME`; the name of the generated `accum_<OP>` |\n| `REPEAT` | `CMakeLists.txt:27` `set(REPEAT \"5\" …)`; `mdmacros.h:30` fallback `5` | `0`..`7` (`REP0`..`REP7` are the only ones defined) | `RUN_LOOP` → the unrolled `REP<REPEAT>` body used by `helper_call` and by `main`; also the argument `main` passes to `use_generated(REPEAT)` |\n\nCross-product: **3 × 8 = 24** build configurations. In the Rust crate these are\nthe Cargo features `add`/`sub`/`mul` × `\"0\"`..`\"7\"`.\n\n### Input-shape axes (per entry point)\n\n| entry point | signature | shapes the code distinguishes |\n|-------------|-----------|-------------------------------|\n| `op_add` / `op_sub` / `op_mul` | `int(int,int)` | zero, positive, negative, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, overflowing pairs, randomized full-range |\n| `helper_call` | `int(int,int)` | same as above; additionally the *return* composes `OP_FN(a,b) + REP<REPEAT>` so it depends on `REPEAT` too, **and it prints two values** |\n| `helper_ptr` | `int(int,int)` | same as above, dispatched through a local function pointer; **prints one value** |\n| `use_generated` | `int(int)` | `n` ∈ `switch` domain `0..=6` (7 distinct in-range shapes) **and** the `default` shape (`n<0`, `n>6`) — see ERRORS.md |\n| `G_OP` (data slot) | `int(*)(int,int)` | dereferenced and called; must equal the `op_<OP>` address for the selected `OP` |\n| `G_OP_NAME` (data slot) | `const char *` | dereferenced as a NUL-terminated string; must equal `STR(OP)` |\n| `main` (whole program) | `argv` | `argc` = 1/2/3/4; operands: decimal, signed, leading blanks, trailing garbage, empty, `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`, out-of-`long` values |\n\n## Configuration table\n\nOne row per meaningful combination the C treats differently. `<op>` ranges over\n`add`, `sub`, `mul`; `<r>` over `0..7`. Every row is exercised for **all 24**\n`(OP, REPEAT)` builds by the differential tests, with many randomized inputs per\nrow (fixed seed, SplitMix64) — not a single hand-picked value.\n\n| #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | ✔ |\n|----|----------------|--------------------------------------------|---|\n| 1  | `op_add` | any `(OP,REPEAT)` build — `op_add` is defined unconditionally; 512 randomized full-range `(a,b)` pairs | [ ] |\n| 2  | `op_add` | boundary operands: `(0,0)`, `(0,±1)`, `(INT_MAX,1)`, `(INT_MIN,-1)`, `(INT_MAX,INT_MAX)`, `(INT_MIN,INT_MIN)` | [ ] |\n| 3  | `op_sub` | any build; 512 randomized full-range `(a,b)` pairs | [ ] |\n| 4  | `op_sub` | boundary operands incl. `(INT_MIN,1)`, `(INT_MAX,-1)`, `(INT_MIN,INT_MAX)` | [ ] |\n| 5  | `op_mul` | any build; 512 randomized full-range `(a,b)` pairs | [ ] |\n| 6  | `op_mul` | boundary operands incl. `(INT_MIN,-1)`, `(INT_MAX,INT_MAX)`, `(INT_MIN,INT_MIN)`, `(x,0)`, `(x,1)` | [ ] |\n| 7  | `G_OP` data slot | `OP=add` build → slot must equal `dlsym(\"op_add\")`, and calling through it must match `op_add` on randomized inputs | [ ] |\n| 8  | `G_OP` data slot | `OP=sub` build → slot must equal `dlsym(\"op_sub\")`; call parity on randomized inputs | [ ] |\n| 9  | `G_OP` data slot | `OP=mul` build → slot must equal `dlsym(\"op_mul\")`; call parity on randomized inputs | [ ] |\n| 10 | `G_OP_NAME` data slot | `OP=add` → C string `\"add\"` (byte-for-byte incl. NUL) | [ ] |\n| 11 | `G_OP_NAME` data slot | `OP=sub` → C string `\"sub\"` | [ ] |\n| 12 | `G_OP_NAME` data slot | `OP=mul` → C string `\"mul\"` | [ ] |\n| 13 | `helper_ptr` | every `(OP,REPEAT)`; 256 randomized `(a,b)` — return value parity | [ ] |\n| 14 | `helper_ptr` | every `(OP,REPEAT)`; **captured stdout** must be byte-identical (`helper.ptr=<r>\\n`), incl. negative and `INT_MIN` results | [ ] |\n| 15 | `helper_call` | `OP=add`, `REPEAT` = 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 (each build) — return `= a+b + (0+1+…+r-1)`; 256 randomized `(a,b)` | [ ] |\n| 16 | `helper_call` | `OP=sub`, `REPEAT` = 0..7 — return `= a-b − (0+1+…+r-1)`; 256 randomized `(a,b)` | [ ] |\n| 17 | `helper_call` | `OP=mul`, `REPEAT` = 0..7 — return `= a*b + r!` (acc starts at `INIT_mul=1`); 256 randomized `(a,b)` | [ ] |\n| 18 | `helper_call` | every build; **captured stdout** byte-identical (`helper.call=<r> helper.acc=<acc>\\n`) | [ ] |\n| 19 | `use_generated` | every build; `n` = 0 (`REP0`, empty body → returns `INIT`) | [ ] |\n| 20 | `use_generated` | every build; `n` = 1,2,3,4,5 (each `switch` case, i.e. each `REPn` unroll depth) | [ ] |\n| 21 | `use_generated` | every build; `n` = 6 (highest in-range case) | [ ] |\n| 22 | `use_generated` | every build; `n` swept over the full `-8..=16` window plus 256 randomized `i32` values — covers in-range, boundary and `default:` shapes in one property test | [ ] |\n| 23 | `use_generated` | every build; **captured stdout** byte-identical (`gen.acc=<r>\\n`) for all `n` in row 22 | [ ] |\n| 24 | composed pipeline (low-level, driven like `main`) | every build: `G_OP(a,b)` → `helper_call(a,b)` → `helper_ptr(a,b)` → `use_generated(REPEAT)`, all four calls in `main`'s order on the *same* library handle, summing the results exactly as `mdmain.c:46` does; 128 randomized `(a,b)`. Verifies call-order-dependent state and the interleaved stdout of the whole sequence | [ ] |\n| 25 | composed pipeline, stdout | every build; the concatenated stdout of the row-24 sequence must be byte-identical (4 lines, correct order) | [ ] |\n| 26 | whole program (`driver` binary) | every build × argument vectors: `3 4`, `0 0`, `-5 9`, `INT_MAX 1`, `INT_MIN -1`, `INT_MAX INT_MAX`, `+8 -8`, extra 4th arg — stdout + stderr + exit status byte-identical | [ ] |\n| 27 | default configuration | no `-DOP` / `-DREPEAT` at all (C `#ifndef` fallbacks) vs `cargo` `--features add,5`, i.e. Cargo `default` — must equal the explicit `OP=add REPEAT=5` build | [ ] |\n| 28 | Rust-only degenerate feature sets | no OP feature / no REPEAT feature / conflicting OP features / conflicting REPEAT features — must still compile and must resolve to the documented priority (`add > sub > mul`, lowest `REPEAT` wins) | [ ] |\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2804,"cache_read_input_tokens":49851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2804,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68928bdc-9013-498f-aad7-5cd065359840","uuid":"7bb15994-33ef-44ab-add5-26d13ad09210","timestamp":"2026-09-02T11:53:35.801Z"}
