{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_davleklws7avoyi2cxynkt4aqm3ytob5qep2vtrz6q6samukhnzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **The Rust translation is byte-identical to the C for every input and every configuration tested.**\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` symbol diff | **empty** for all 24 configs; 0 unresolved non-libc symbols |\n| Phase B — `CONFIGS.md` | **28/28 rows** pass across randomized inputs |\n| Phase C — `ERRORS.md` | **12/12 rows** have a passing error-path differential test |\n| Every feature combination | 96 `cargo check` combos compile; 24 canonical + 14 degenerate feature sets pass all 34 tests |\n\n## What was found\n\nThe translation was already behaviorally correct — no divergences surfaced. One real defect fixed:\n\n- **`src/mdmacros.rs` was orphaned dead code with contradictory logic.** No `mod mdmacros;` existed in `lib.rs` or `main.rs`, so it was never compiled, and its cascade resolved `OP` as `mul > sub > add` with *highest*-`REPEAT`-wins — the opposite of the live `mdconfig.rs` (`add > sub > mul`, lowest wins). Aligned it, wired it into `lib.rs` so it's compile-checked, and added a unit test that fails if the two ever drift.\n\nTwo things worth noting about the C surface:\n- `CMakeLists.txt` builds **only an executable**, no `.so`. The library half is `mdcore.c` (`mdmain.c` holds `main`), so the harness compiles that TU standalone with `-fPIC -shared`. `c_src` was not modified.\n- `REP7` exists in `mdmacros.h` but is **not** a `switch` case in `DISPATCH_REP`, so `use_generated(7)` hits `default: break` and returns `INIT_FOR(OP)` even in a `REPEAT=7` build. The Rust matches; `err04` pins this.\n\n## Test design\n\n`tests/` loads both `.so`s via `libloading` and never calls the Rust crate directly, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are under test. Since all three helpers `printf`, the harness captures fd 1 (`dup2` + `fflush(NULL)`) and compares **printed bytes**, not just return values. Data symbols `G_OP`/`G_OP_NAME` are checked for pointer *identity* against `dlsym(\"op_<OP>\")`, not merely behavior.\n\nTo guard against a vacuous suite, `scripts/negative_control.sh` injects 8 deliberate mutations (off-by-one on the switch domain, wrong `INIT_mul`, hardwired `G_OP`, printf spacing drift, `run_loop` off-by-one, saturating instead of wrapping arithmetic, missing print, wrong `G_OP_NAME`) — **all 8 are detected**, and the pristine tree passes again afterward.\n\nRe-run everything with `bash scripts/verify_all.sh`. Note: `cargo` needs `CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true` here since crates.io is unreachable through the proxy; `libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local registry cache."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":117092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":432,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68928bdc-9013-498f-aad7-5cd065359840","uuid":"19926d0b-0ccd-4945-94e8-140d4525340f","timestamp":"2026-09-02T12:06:14.151Z"}
